<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoNodeGetValue</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Get the value of a leaf node.</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Node.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">const SilikoValue *SilikoNodeGetValue(
    const SilikoNode *object);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoNodeGetValue</function> retrieves the value
of <varname>object</varname> if <varname>object</varname> is a leaf
node. To get the effective value of a branch node, use
<function>SilikoEvaluate</function> instead.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para><function>SilikoNodeGetValue</function> returns a pointer to
the <type>SilikoValue</type> object held by <varname>object</varname>
if <varname>object</varname> is a leaf node, <literal>NULL</literal>
otherwise. If <function>SilikoNodeGetValue</function> returns a valid
pointer, the object point to is still owned by
<varname>object</varname> and must not be deallocated.</para>
</refsection>
